      <method name="create_source"
              c:identifier="g_datagram_based_create_source"
              version="2.48">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gdatagrambased.c"
             line="311">Creates a #GSource that can be attached to a #GMainContext to monitor for
the availability of the specified @condition on the #GDatagramBased. The
#GSource keeps a reference to the @datagram_based.

The callback on the source is of the #GDatagramBasedSourceFunc type.

It is meaningless to specify %G_IO_ERR or %G_IO_HUP in @condition; these
conditions will always be reported in the callback if they are true.

If non-%NULL, @cancellable can be used to cancel the source, which will
cause the source to trigger, reporting the current condition (which is
likely 0 unless cancellation happened at the same time as a condition
change). You can check for this in the callback using
g_cancellable_is_cancelled().</doc>
