              c:type="G_FILE_ATTRIBUTE_STANDARD_ALLOCATED_SIZE"
              version="2.20">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gio/gfileinfo.h"
           line="240">A key in the "standard" namespace for getting the amount of disk space
that is consumed by the file (in bytes).

This will generally be larger than the file size (due to block size
overhead) but can occasionally be smaller (for example, for sparse files).

Corresponding #GFileAttributeType is %G_FILE_ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_UINT64.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gio/gfileinfo.h" line="253"/>
      <type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
