      <virtual-method name="replace_readwrite"
                      invoker="replace_readwrite"
                      version="2.22"
                      throws="1"
                      glib:async-func="replace_readwrite_async">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gfile.c"
             line="2043">Returns an output stream for overwriting the file in readwrite mode,
possibly creating a backup copy of the file first. If the file doesn't
exist, it will be created.

For details about the behaviour, see g_file_replace() which does the
same thing but returns an output stream only.

Note that in many non-local file cases read and write streams are not
supported, so make sure you really need to do read and write streaming,
rather than just opening for reading or writing.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gfile.h" line="510"/>
