      <virtual-method name="set_display_name"
                      invoker="set_display_name"
                      throws="1"
                      glib:async-func="set_display_name_async">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gfile.c"
             line="4845">Renames @file to the specified display name.

The display name is converted from UTF-8 to the correct encoding
for the target filesystem if possible and the @file is renamed to this.

If you want to implement a rename operation in the user interface the
edit name (%G_FILE_ATTRIBUTE_STANDARD_EDIT_NAME) should be used as the
initial value in the rename widget, and then the result after editing
should be passed to g_file_set_display_name().

On success the resulting converted filename is returned.

If @cancellable is not %NULL, then the operation can be cancelled by
triggering the cancellable object from another thread. If the operation
was cancelled, the error %G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED will be returned.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gfile.h" line="241"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gio/gfile.c"
