                 filename="gio/gsettingsschema.c"
                 line="249">a #GSettingsSchemaSource, or %NULL</doc>
            <type name="SettingsSchemaSource" c:type="GSettingsSchemaSource*"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="trusted" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gio/gsettingsschema.c"
                 line="250">%TRUE, if the directory is trusted</doc>
            <type name="gboolean" c:type="gboolean"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </constructor>
      <method name="list_schemas"
              c:identifier="g_settings_schema_source_list_schemas"
              version="2.40">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gsettingsschema.c"
             line="754">Lists the schemas in a given source.

If @recursive is %TRUE then include parent sources.  If %FALSE then
only include the schemas from one source (ie: one directory).  You
probably want %TRUE.

Non-relocatable schemas are those for which you can call
g_settings_new().  Relocatable schemas are those for which you must
use g_settings_new_with_path().

Do not call this function from normal programs.  This is designed for
use by database editors, commandline tools, etc.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gsettingsschema.h" line="56"/>
