      <method name="get_successful"
              c:identifier="g_subprocess_get_successful"
              version="2.40">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gsubprocess.c"
             line="1118">Checks if the process was "successful".  A process is considered
successful if it exited cleanly with an exit status of 0, either by
way of the exit() system call or return from main().

It is an error to call this function before g_subprocess_wait() has
returned.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gsubprocess.h" line="111"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gio/gsubprocess.c"
               line="1129">%TRUE if the process exited cleanly with a exit status of 0</doc>
          <type name="gboolean" c:type="gboolean"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="subprocess" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gio/gsubprocess.c"
                 line="1120">a #GSubprocess</doc>
            <type name="Subprocess" c:type="GSubprocess*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="get_term_sig"
              c:identifier="g_subprocess_get_term_sig"
              version="2.40">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gsubprocess.c"
             line="1235">Get the signal number that caused the subprocess to terminate, given
that it terminated due to a signal.

This is equivalent to the system WTERMSIG macro.

It is an error to call this function before g_subprocess_wait() and
unless g_subprocess_get_if_signaled() returned %TRUE.</doc>
