      <method name="set_stdout_file_path"
              c:identifier="g_subprocess_launcher_set_stdout_file_path"
              version="2.40">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gsubprocesslauncher.c"
             line="470">Sets the file path to use as the stdout for spawned processes.

If @path is %NULL then any previously given path is unset.

The file will be created or truncated when the process is spawned, as
would be the case if using '&gt;' at the shell.

You may not set a stdout file path if a stdout fd is already set or
if the launcher flags contain any flags directing stdout elsewhere.

This feature is only available on UNIX.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gsubprocesslauncher.h" line="91"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
