              version="2.36"
              throws="1">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gtask.c"
             line="1875">Gets the result of @task as a pointer, and transfers ownership
of that value to the caller.

If the task resulted in an error, or was cancelled, then this will
instead return %NULL and set @error.

Since this method transfers ownership of the return value (or
error) to the caller, you may only call it once.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gtask.h" line="192"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="full" nullable="1">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gio/gtask.c"
               line="1889">the task result, or %NULL on error</doc>
          <type name="gpointer" c:type="gpointer"/>
