              glib:set-property="advertised-protocols"
              version="2.60">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gtlsconnection.c"
             line="808">Sets the list of application-layer protocols to advertise that the
caller is willing to speak on this connection. The
Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN) extension will be
used to negotiate a compatible protocol with the peer; use
g_tls_connection_get_negotiated_protocol() to find the negotiated
protocol after the handshake.  Specifying %NULL for the the value
of @protocols will disable ALPN negotiation.

See [IANA TLS ALPN Protocol IDs](https://www.iana.org/assignments/tls-extensiontype-values/tls-extensiontype-values.xhtml#alpn-protocol-ids)
for a list of registered protocol IDs.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gtlsconnection.h" line="146"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
