      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gio/gunixfdlist.c"
           line="17">A `GUnixFDList` contains a list of file descriptors.  It owns the file
descriptors that it contains, closing them when finalized.

It may be wrapped in a
[`GUnixFDMessage`](../gio-unix/class.UnixFDMessage.html) and sent over a
[class@Gio.Socket] in the `G_SOCKET_FAMILY_UNIX` family by using
[method@Gio.Socket.send_message] and received using
[method@Gio.Socket.receive_message].

Before 2.74, `&lt;gio/gunixfdlist.h&gt;` belonged to the UNIX-specific GIO
interfaces, thus you had to use the `gio-unix-2.0.pc` pkg-config file when
using it.

Since 2.74, the API is available for Windows.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gio/gunixfdlist.h" line="58"/>
      <constructor name="new" c:identifier="g_unix_fd_list_new" version="2.24">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gunixfdlist.c"
             line="151">Creates a new #GUnixFDList containing no file descriptors.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gio/gunixfdlist.h" line="69"/>
