    <function name="content_type_guess_for_tree"
              c:identifier="g_content_type_guess_for_tree"
              version="2.18">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gio/gcontenttype.c"
           line="352">Tries to guess the type of the tree with root @root, by
looking at the files it contains. The result is an array
of content types, with the best guess coming first.

The types returned all have the form x-content/foo, e.g.
x-content/audio-cdda (for audio CDs) or x-content/image-dcf
(for a camera memory card). See the
[shared-mime-info](http://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Specifications/shared-mime-info-spec)
specification for more on x-content types.

This function is useful in the implementation of
g_mount_guess_content_type().</doc>
      <source-position filename="gio/gcontenttype.h" line="69"/>
      <return-value transfer-ownership="full">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gcontenttype.c"
             line="369">an %NULL-terminated
    array of zero or more content types. Free with g_strfreev()</doc>
        <array c:type="gchar**">
          <type name="utf8"/>
        </array>
      </return-value>
      <parameters>
        <parameter name="root" transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gio/gcontenttype.c"
               line="354">the root of the tree to guess a type for</doc>
          <type name="File" c:type="GFile*"/>
        </parameter>
      </parameters>
    </function>
