    <function name="pollable_stream_read"
              c:identifier="g_pollable_stream_read"
              version="2.34"
              throws="1">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gio/gpollableutils.c"
           line="163">Tries to read from @stream, as with g_input_stream_read() (if
@blocking is %TRUE) or g_pollable_input_stream_read_nonblocking()
(if @blocking is %FALSE). This can be used to more easily share
code between blocking and non-blocking implementations of a method.

If @blocking is %FALSE, then @stream must be a
#GPollableInputStream for which g_pollable_input_stream_can_poll()
returns %TRUE, or else the behavior is undefined. If @blocking is
%TRUE, then @stream does not need to be a #GPollableInputStream.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gio/gpollableutils.h" line="41"/>
      <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gio/gpollableutils.c"
             line="183">the number of bytes read, or -1 on error.</doc>
